ask18: export 5 SDK symbols consumed by the cdx OOT module

The cdx OOT module (sourced from we-are-mono/ASK, authored against the
lf-6.12.y SDK overlay) references five SDK helpers that lf-6.6.y defines
but does not EXPORT_SYMBOL.  Without an exported symbol, modpost flags
each as undefined when the cdx.ko is linked, regardless of whether the
referenced functions are actually reachable on the boot path.

Add EXPORT_SYMBOL (or EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL where the surrounding qbman
file already uses the GPL variant) immediately after each function
definition.  This is parity with lf-6.12.y's own export set; we are
not inventing new exports.

Symbols added:
- FM_PORT_PcdPlcrAllocProfiles      (sdk_fman/.../fm_port.c)
- FM_VSP_Config                     (sdk_fman/.../fm_sp.c)
- FM_VSP_ConfigBufferPrefixContent  (sdk_fman/.../fm_sp.c)
- FM_MURAM_AllocMem                 (sdk_fman/.../fm_muram.c)
- qman_sp_enable_ceetm_mode         (staging/fsl_qbman/qman_config.c)

Closes 5 of 10 modpost ERRORs from the ask17 CI run.

